<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>DW - English for Africa</title><subtitle type="html">News, Analysis and Service from Germany and Europe - in 30 Languages</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-africa</id><updated>2026-10-31T05:58:42Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-africa" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-12756?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-africa" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>UN peacekeeping mission in Western Sahara to expire amid US, Russia vetoes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4c10ae421eef5725ca17b57a846cc89d5677ebcefbc8383571f6df88777f6e90</id><updated>2026-10-31T05:58:42Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T04:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/un-peacekeeping-mission-in-western-sahara-to-expire-amid-us-russia-vetoes/a-79814338--f1640d90bbfc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/un-peacekeeping-mission-in-western-sahara-to-expire-amid-us-russia-vetoes/a-79814338?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The mandate of the UN peacekeeping force in Western Sahara will expire on October 31. The UN Security Council could not agree on a resolution to extend the mission.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Smuggling, power, profit: Irregular migration out of eastern Libya</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:337cfb38eb7210ce23d123c38febc7d5e3505b8fc94328f9df713147de2e75c0</id><updated>2026-10-31T05:57:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T18:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/irregular-migration-from-libya-to-crete-is-rising-raising-questions-about-the-links-between-people-s/a-79808822--583a8979ee7e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/smuggling-power-profit-irregular-migration-out-of-eastern-libya/a-79808822?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">There is currently more irregular migration between eastern Libya and Crete, Greece. It's raising questions as to what connects people smugglers with powerful militias in eastern Libya and then in turn, Europeans.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Bayern Munich's Kenya friendly highlights Africa's growing pull for global sport</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d9a0cfbaf3bf60572b1cd8c17871e8b7d7496a872cc8b16e56331bb7aae603c1</id><updated>2026-10-31T05:57:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T13:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bayern-munich-s-kenya-friendly-highlights-africa-s-growing-pull-for-global-sport/a-79796753--c6f4b50cf1c0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bayern-munich-s-kenya-friendly-highlights-africa-s-growing-pull-for-global-sport/a-79796753?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bayern Munich are to open Nairobi's new Raila Odinga International Stadium against Ajax as Kenya prepares for AFCON 2027. The match highlights Africa's growing sports ambitions — and questions over cost and legacy.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Human trafficking victims stranded in Guinea-Bissau</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b40c3cff8aebde971c3e21571596b51e98f331c71c563e73c5d2458fb0992ae8</id><updated>2026-10-31T05:57:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T14:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/human-trafficking-victims-stranded-in-guinea-bissau/a-79785558--af9688fcc3e2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/human-trafficking-victims-stranded-in-guinea-bissau/a-79785558?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Dozens of West Africans lured to Guinea-Bissau with promises of jobs and migration to Europe say they were exploited by a suspected trafficking network. Now many cannot afford to return home.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
